# tools/repeat_paint_witness.rish -- a REPEATING positioned gradient SEEN on a real image proves itself on metal (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) -- the fourth shape of the CSS gradient family, the sibling of
# tools/gradient_paint_witness.rish (the LINEAR family), tools/radial_paint_witness.rish (the RADIAL circle), and
# tools/conic_paint_witness.rish (the CONIC sweep). This rung proves the REPEATING gradient: the ramp runs over a fixed
# PERIOD of cells and TILES across the strip, so the pattern reads first..last, first..last with a hard seam at each tile
# boundary (the CSS repeating-linear-gradient shape). Stands on the positioned ramp (image/color_ramp_stops.rye), the open
# color algebra (image/color.rye), and the open QOI codec (image/qoi.rye).
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260816/20260816-210735_season-g-color-algebra-crux.md (the color floor this stands on).
# Teacher, thanked clean-room: gratitude/w3c-css-color.md (the W3C CSS Color / Images specs -- public standards only).
#
# The crux this witness proves is that a repeating positioned gradient becomes a real image: paint_gradient_repeat_h fills a
# box where each column is the color the positioned ramp samples at that column's position WITHIN its tile, tiling across the
# strip. A black-to-white ramp over period 4 makes each pixel's red channel equal its tile position, so an 8-wide strip reads
# 0,85,170,255 twice (the ramp tiles); the tile repeats exactly (column 0 equals column period); each tile ascends
# 0<85<170<255 then seams hard (255 drops straight to 0 at the tile boundary); a horizontal repeat is constant down each
# column and the vertical twin tiles the same ramp down the rows; a red-green-blue strip round-trips through the open QOI
# codec byte-for-byte; a wider period spreads the ramp over more cells where a narrow one wraps; a sub-rectangle paints only
# its own box; a zero dimension, a period under two, a period past the dimension ceiling, an out-of-bounds box, and a
# non-ascending ramp refuse by name having painted nothing. Compose not braid -- color_ramp_stops decides the color, qoi owns
# the target, color composites; this rung only routes each cell to its position within its tile. The routing is one integer
# modulo so a tiling is deterministic. No network, no key, no funds.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/repeat_paint_witness.rish

say "repeat-paint: Language EN -- Season G's repeating positioned gradient painted onto an image; a keeper names a stop list and a period and reads back a tiled gradient a surface can show, on our own color model and open codec."
say "repeat-paint: Style Radiant -- compose not braid; color_ramp_stops DECIDES each cell's color, qoi owns the RGBA target, color composites src-over, and this rung only ROUTES each cell to its position within its tile so a translucent tiling tints the picture beneath."
say "repeat-paint: Lens TAME -- the whole box bound-checked ONCE up front in u64 so a far edge can never wrap; the period checked against a named dimension ceiling; the ramp validated ONCE before any pixel so a malformed strip refuses having painted nothing; the tile routed through one integer modulo so a tiling is deterministic; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/repeat_paint"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/repeat_paint.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "repeat-paint: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "repeat-paint: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "repeat-paint: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-repeat-paint" else "repeat-paint: selftest did not print the GREEN repeat-paint line"

assert selftest.out contains "round-trips through the open QOI codec byte-for-byte" else "repeat-paint: the painted strip did not prove its QOI round trip"

assert selftest.out contains "the ramp tiles" else "repeat-paint: the strip did not prove the ramp tiles across the period"

assert selftest.out contains "seams hard" else "repeat-paint: the strip did not prove its hard tile seam"

assert selftest.out contains "a wider period spreads the ramp over more cells" else "repeat-paint: the strip did not prove the period spreads the ramp"

say "repeat-paint: GREEN -- a repeating positioned gradient painted onto a real image, its tiling and hard seam exact, its period a real control, its round trip byte-for-byte, proven on metal."
